## "@ " for mentioning people, teams

To get suggestions for mentions so you don't need to type the whole name. When person or team is mentioned, the conversation will appear in Screener in Desk screen.

### Examples

"@person" - to mention specific person

"@team" - to mention all people in the team

? "@/bug-analyzer what's the issue here?"

## "!" for urgent

To make the message important for person or team that you're mentioning. The message will then be shown in Urgent section on Desk screen.

### Examples

"!@person-name" - mentioned person will get urgent message

"!@team-abc" - everyone in mentioned team will get urgent message

"@person-a !@person-b" - only person be will get urgent message

## "->" for resolutions

To resolve with message the conversation.

### Examples

"->" or "-> done" or "-> resolve" - conversation will be resolved without specific resolution message

"-> We will postpone this feature." - conversation will be resolved with resolution message

## "#tags" for tagging

To label conversation or topic with tag.

### Examples

"some text #tag-name some text" - conversation now is assigned under tag

## "# topic title" for creating / assigning to topic

One first line to create or assign topic.

In the middle of text as way to reference current topic.

